not last ...","title":"The fabric of life: what if mosquito nets were durable and widely available but insecticide-free? - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7370456/"},{"position":6,"site_name":"www.cdcfoundation.org","snippet":"An insecticide-treated bed net protects the person sleeping under the net even if the net has small holes in it, because the insecticide kills mosquitoes that ...","title":"Bed Nets for Children","url":"https://www.cdcfoundation.org/bednets"},{"date":"Jul 12, 2021","position":7,"site_name":"apmen.org","snippet":"... treated bednets are now ineffective ... not very strong evidence to suggest that increasing insecticide resistance makes ITN's less effective.","title":"Much discussion about bednets","url":"https://apmen.org/resources/much-discussion-about-bednets"},{"position":8,"site_name":"en.wikipedia.org","snippet":"ITNs are estimated to be twice as effective as untreated nets, [23] and offer greater than 70% protection compared with no net.","title":"Mosquito net","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mosquito_net"},{"date":"Jul 21, 2025","position":9,"site_name":"ccp.jhu.edu","snippet":"CCP research finds that Tanzanians can only buy untreated nets, which are less effective at malaria prevention than treated ones.","title":"Study: Gold Standard of Mosquito Nets Not Sold in Tanzanian Markets","url":"https://ccp.jhu.edu/2025/07/21/untreated-nets-malaria-tanzania-study/"}],"total_results":9,"page":0}